    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change accepts an optional `title` on owner creation and returns a computed `salutation` (`title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given).\n\nI kept structural impact minimal \u2014 **2 files, no edits to any complex method**:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema. The generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` pick these up by convention (`title` \u2192 `Owner.title`, `Owner.getSalutation()` \u2192 DTO), so no mapper or controller code changed.\n\n2. **`Person.java`** (the small base class, low surrounding complexity \u2014 not the large `Owner` class) \u2014 added a `@Transient` `title` field with its accessors and a tiny `getSalutation()` composing the value. `title` lives beside `firstName`/`lastName`, the natural home, and stays transient (request-scoped) so no schema/DDL changes were needed.\n\nI avoided touching `Owner`, `OwnerMapper`, and the controllers entirely \u2014 the two highest-WMC surfaces \u2014 by relying on OpenAPI generation and MapStruct's by-name auto-mapping.",
